  { question: "Can I take cannabis across state lines from Maine?", answer: "No. Transporting cannabis across state lines is a federal offense, even between two states where it is legal. You must consume or dispose of any cannabis before leaving Maine. The same applies to air travel — cannabis is illegal in airports and on aircraft under federal law." },
  { question: "How much weed can you carry in Maine?", answer: "Adults 21+ may lawfully possess up to 2.5 ounces of cannabis, or a combination of cannabis and concentrate, under 28-B M.R.S. §1501. Within that total, no more than 10 grams may be concentrate. Possessing more than the legal limit is a crime — under 17-A M.R.S. §1107-A, knowingly possessing over 2.5 ounces (up to 8 ounces) is a Class E crime, not a civil infraction. Medical patients and caregivers have separate, higher possession limits under the medical program." },
  { question: "Can tourists buy weed in Maine?", answer: "Yes. Maine does not require residency for adult-use purchases. A tourist age 21 or older with a valid government-issued photo ID (driver's license or passport from any state or country) can buy cannabis at a licensed adult-use dispensary. Out-of-state medical cards from Maine's approved reciprocity states also work at medical dispensaries — see our <a href=\"/guides/maine-out-of-state-patient-reciprocity\">visiting-patient reciprocity guide</a> for the approved-state list." },
